"""
RAILWAY OBSTACLE DETECTION - ALL-IN-ONE DASHBOARD  (single file, version 4.1)

COMBINED DETECTION LOGIC:
  - Obstacle is detected using TF-Luna LiDAR, HC-SR04 Ultrasonic, AND 5MP Camera.
  - LiDAR or ultrasonic <= SLOW_CM (or ultrasonic sudden drop), OR camera detects an obstacle
    when CAM_DETECT_ACTIVE=True -> speed reduces smoothly to 0 -> camera identifies/labels
    the object -> stays stopped until sensors read beyond SLOW_CM + CLEAR_MARGIN_CM (and
    camera is clear) for 1 s, then press Start.
  - Important info is shown on the 16x2 LCD and live web dashboard.

Raspberry Pi 4 (2 GB) + TF-Luna LiDAR + HC-SR04 + Pi Camera (5 MP) + L298N + DC geared motor

RUN:      python3 railwayproject2.py          then open  http://<pi-ip>:5000
INSTALL:  sudo apt update
          sudo apt install -y python3-flask python3-opencv python3-numpy python3-serial \
                              python3-gpiozero python3-lgpio python3-picamera2 python3-smbus i2c-tools
          sudo raspi-config -> Interface Options -> I2C -> Enable -> reboot
          sudo raspi-config -> Interface Options -> Serial Port -> login shell: NO, serial hardware: YES -> reboot

OPTIONAL YOLO (names animals: cow, giraffe, elephant, horse, dog, person ...). Download once:
          cd ~/RailwayProject/models
          wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AlexeyAB/darknet/master/cfg/yolov4-tiny.cfg
          wget https://github.com/AlexeyAB/darknet/releases/download/darknet_yolo_v4_pre/yolov4-tiny.weights

HOW THE CAMERA LEARNS YOUR OBJECTS
  Every folder inside  dataset/  is one class. The folder name is the label shown on the dashboard.
  A folder whose name contains the word "clear" means "no obstacle".  Any other folder = an obstacle type.
  Example:  dataset/clear_no_obstacle   dataset/cow   dataset/buffalo   dataset/giraffe_toy
  Capture images with the dashboard, then press "Train from dataset".

WIRING (physical pin numbers of the 40-pin header)
  HC-SR04   VCC -> Pin 2 (5V)   GND -> Pin 6   TRIG -> Pin 16 (GPIO23)
            ECHO -> voltage divider (1k + 2k) -> Pin 18 (GPIO24)
  TF-Luna   VCC -> Pin 4 (5V)   GND -> Pin 14   TX -> Pin 10 (GPIO15 RXD)   RX -> Pin 8 (GPIO14 TXD)
  L298N     ENA + ENB (both) -> Pin 12 (GPIO18)   IN1 -> Pin 29 (GPIO5)   IN3 -> Pin 31 (GPIO6)
            IN2 and IN4 -> GND (important, do not leave them floating)   GND -> Pin 20 + battery minus
  Pi Camera ribbon cable -> CSI camera port
  LCD 16x2 I2C  VCC -> 5V   GND -> GND   SDA -> Pin 3 (GPIO2)   SCL -> Pin 5 (GPIO3)   (address 0x27 or 0x3F, auto-detected)
"""
